{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line of $2.00 on TRP-02815 is charged for a gantry the GPS trace never crosses (nearest fix 6,130.08 m away, far outside the 250 m match radius); record it as a billing-integrity finding, refund it as a standalone pass-through correction, and review why the line was charged."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. Your dispute was over $4.00, and $2.00 of it is returned to the rider.\n\nRoute deviation — not established. The measurement that governs is the GPS trace, 13.65 km, not the trip record's rounded 13.7 km. Against the booked optimal of 13.0 km the excess is 0.65 km, or 5.0%, and POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be BOTH more than 0.8 km and more than 20% of optimal. Neither gate is passed, so no deviation exists, POL-RD-02 is never reached, and no distance or time refund is due. The driver's submissions on this point are accepted in full.\n\nThe ERP line — $2.00 refunded. The fare ledger carries a single ERP line, 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry', at $2.00. That gantry carries coordinates, and the driver's own trace (108 fixes, 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps) never comes within the 250 m match radius of it — the nearest fix is 6,130.08 m away, on a Yishun-to-Bishan trip that runs nowhere near the AYE. The vehicle never crossed this gantry. POL-RD-09(4) makes a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction and available whether or not a deviation exists. The rider's claim succeeds on this line and $2.00 is returned. The driver's statement that 'the ERP is charged by the system' names no evidence ID and no clause; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and does not show a crossing.\n\nThe rest of the $4.00 — the remaining $2.00 of the contested amount corresponds to no identified line of the fare breakdown, so it is not refunded.\n\nFigures used: charged_total $21.86; the refunded ERP line $2.00; optimal_route_erp_sgd $0.00; traced excess 0.65 km / 5.0%; amount contested $4.00.\n\nNo escalation. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c); the trip identifiers all match; the only charge line with no counterpart in the trace is the one already refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-09 states does not trigger POL-RD-10(8); and no party has invoked the missing advisory EV-ADVIS-02815-01 (admissibility MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) as an excuse — it is cited only for its absence, so POL-RD-13(1) and POL-RD-10(5) do not engage.\n\nThe ruling rests on the GPS trace and the fare breakdown, both at weight 1.0, so it is not discounted on confidence. The POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral rides alongside the money and does not displace it. This ruling is provisional; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the single ERP line on EV-FARE-02815, 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry', SGD 2.00 charged at 2026-09-08T12:47:55, is charged for a gantry the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02815) never crosses — nearest of 108 fixes is 6,130.08 m, far outside the 250 m match radius, and the platform's own routing records it on_optimal_route = false with optimal-route ERP of 0.00. Refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction; POL-RD-10(8) is not thereby triggered."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider, this ruling returns SGD 2.00 of the SGD 4.00 you contested, on billing integrity rather than on route deviation. — Route deviation: not established. Measured on the governing field (EV-GPS-02815.trace_distance_km = 13.65 km, which POL-RD-01 makes govern over the rounded trip-record 13.7 km), the excess over the booked optimal of 13.0 km is 0.65 km, or 5.0%. POL-RD-01 requires excess greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% of optimal; both must pass and neither does. No deviation exists, so POL-RD-02 never runs and the metered distance charge (10.28) and time charge (4.98) on EV-FARE-02815 stand. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes — 108 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps — so POL-RD-07 does not fire. — ERP line: this is where your claim succeeds. The fare breakdown carries one ERP line, 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry', SGD 2.00, charged at 12:47:55. The platform's own routing marks that gantry on_optimal_route = false with optimal-route ERP of 0.00, and the driver's trace never comes near it: the closest fix is 6,130.08 m away, against the 250 m radius by which POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace. The vehicle did not cross that gantry. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge for a gantry the trace never passed is a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. That is the SGD 2.00. The remaining SGD 2.00 of the SGD 4.00 you contested corresponds to no line on the fare breakdown and no artifact identifies it, so it cannot be returned; the refund is therefore partial. — Driver, your points are accepted: no deviation is established; POL-RD-02 does not run; your trailing-90-day record (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 388 completed trips, EV-DPROF-02815) means POL-RD-06 furnishes no uplift and no conduct referral, and the correction is confined to the pass-through lines. Your statement that 'the ERP is charged by the system' names no evidence ID and cannot show the vehicle ever crossed the gantry, so under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight against the trace. No traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-02815-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing, and under POL-RD-13 the absence of an advisory no one cited is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction and not an escalation. — No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), the trip identifiers and timestamps agree across EV-TRIP-02815, EV-GPS-02815 and EV-FARE-02815, the refund is far below SGD 150.00, and the only unmatched charge line is one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-09 expressly excludes from POL-RD-10(8). The monetary effect is SGD 2.00, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes automatically, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04. Confidence rests on EV-GPS-02815 and EV-FARE-02815, both at weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity — the $2.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line charged on trip TRP-02815 is refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction: the GPS trace never comes within the 250 m gantry match radius (nearest fix 6,130.08 m), so the line is charged for a crossing that did not happen. Review the fare ledger's ERP sourcing for this trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and Driver — this rules on the disputed charge on trip TRP-02815.\n\nRoute deviation: none. POL-RD-01 provides that the trace figure governs and the rounded trip_record copy may not be cited; gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 13.65 km against a booked optimal of 13.0 km, an excess of 0.65 km and 5.00%. Both establishment tests must pass and neither does — 0.65 km is under the 0.8 km absolute gate and 5.00% is under the 20% proportional gate. No deviation is established, so POL-RD-02 never runs and no distance-or-time refund (base fare, distance charge 9.75, time charge 4.98) arises. The driver's first two claims are accepted on this point.\n\nERP line: refunded in full, $2.00. The fare ledger carries exactly one ERP line: $2.00 for the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' (lat 1.366147, lng 103.754636). POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. The driver's own trace — 108 fixes, 100.0% coverage, 10-second sampling, zero gaps — comes no closer than 6,130.08 m. The vehicle never crossed this gantry, so the line is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists, and recorded as a billing-integrity referral. Figures used: the money block's erp_lines total $2.00 (off_optimal_route_total $2.00; on_optimal_route_total $0.00), against charged_total $21.86.\n\nThe driver's answer, 'The ERP is charged by the system', cites no evidence id and no artifact showing the gantry was crossed; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight against the trace. It is not an external-traffic-cause assertion backed by an advisory, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged (POL-RD-13(1)), and the bundle's only advisory, EV-ADVIS-02815-01 (admissibility MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0), is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c); and the only unmatched charge line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) excludes by its terms. The rider's claims that the case be ruled rather than held are accepted.\n\nPOL-RD-06 is not consulted because no material deviation exists, and its trailing-90-day counters would not fire in any event (0 flags over 388 trips), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral.\n\nOutcome: of the $4.00 contested, $2.00 is returned — a PARTIAL_REFUND. The balance corresponds to no identified line on the fare breakdown and is not recoverable. The $2.00 monetary effect is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00 and executes automatically on issue. Both parties retain the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
